Hi Meera,

Ahead of our 14:00 BST discussion, I have attached the decision paper and Con=
nor's separate summary workbook.

The two counts answer different questions. The supplier selection covers 12 o=
f 42 suppliers, ranked on Q1 posted net purchases. The exception review cover=
s 93 requests received across suppliers from April to June; the reason breakd=
own is for the 37 marked urgent at submission, not for the 12 selected suppli=
ers or all 93 requests. The workbook contains the aggregate counts, not indiv=
idual request details. Please come to me if you would like to follow up a par=
ticular request.

The paper compares reopening negotiations across the supplier base with devel=
oping the demand handoff to Buying first. Our recommendation is to work on de=
mand sharing first, while retaining the existing exception route for demand a=
rising after the cut-off and supplier changes. The evidence does not yet tell=
 us how many exceptions the handoff would avoid.

At the meeting, I would like to agree the order in which to develop the impro=
vements and identify a Buying contact to work with Neha on the handoff. We ca=
n then work through the fields and the treatment of unknown times before sett=
ing a start date.

Best,
Nicholas

